nfsshift-mp (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the crash when tapping the "ready" check mark in the lobby after
    choosing a car. The game's screen element lookup (0x4a0a2fc4) compares
    its index signed, so the -1 it is handed for elements the Wi-Fi lobby
    layout does not have reached array[-1] on a screen without elements
    (a read of 0xfffffffc). A one-word patch makes the compare unsigned; the
    function already returns for -1 on that path.
  * Fix the crash at the green light. Opponent samples were inserted into the
    game's history vector straight from the s3eDeviceYield hook. When that
    vector grew, the game's allocation went through the runtime's stack-switch
    thunk and overwrote the hook's own live stack frames with the allocation
    size (0xa4, 0x148). Samples are now queued and inserted when the game
    itself calls one of the multiplayer stubs - the same call context in which
    the game does its own allocations. A full race inserted all 2408 samples
    without dropping one.
  * Print a crash report on SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL, SIGFPE and SIGABRT:
    registers, pc and lr mapped to game addresses, and the call chain found on
    the stack. The game still dies as before. Started from a shell,
    NFSMP_LOG=/home/user/nfsmp.log /opt/nfsshift-mp/startup-mp.sh keeps it.
  * Known issue: with the N9 as a guest (joining another device's session) the
    game still crashes before the race has loaded. Hosting a race works, and
    the Sailfish OS and Android ports join an N9 host without problems.

 -- smatkovi <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:20:00 +0200

nfsshift-mp (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * First release: LAN multiplayer transport for the MeeGo build of NFS Shift,
    loaded with LD_PRELOAD next to the untouched original package. Up to four
    players, cross-play with the Sailfish OS and Android ports.

 -- smatkovi <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:37:00 +0200
